  "body": {
    "id": "lem:stable-certified-padding",
    "kind": "lemma",
    "statement": "Let \\(\\delta_n=2^{-p_n-1}\\), and, on \\(\\kappa_n=0\\), let \\(\\mathcal B_n\\) be the coordinate box of radius \\(\\delta_n\\) about \\((\\widetilde X,\\widetilde R,\\widetilde C)\\).  The certificate in \\(H_n^{\\mathrm{cert}}\\) can be chosen so that there are finite constants \\(K_\\star\\) and \\(k_\\star\\), depending only on \\(c,C_0,B,\\sigma,r_0\\), for which the following holds for all sufficiently large \\(n>r_0\\).  If every coordinate of the box is at most \\(T_n^{\\mathrm{enc}}+1\\) in absolute value, then\n\\[\n0\\le\\Delta_n^{\\mathrm{enc}}+\\Delta_n^{\\mathrm{arith}}\n\\le K_\\star(n+T_n^{\\mathrm{enc}}+\\alpha^{-1}+1)^{k_\\star}.\n\\]\nIf in addition every donor matrix \\(X'\\) in the box satisfies\n\\[\ns_r(X')\\ge3cn/4,\\qquad s_{r+1}(X')\\le cn/4,\n\\qquad s_1(X')\\le3C_0n/2,\n\\]\nthen\n\\[\n\\Delta_n^{\\mathrm{enc}}+\\Delta_n^{\\mathrm{arith}}\n\\le K_\\star(n+T_n^{\\mathrm{enc}}+\\alpha^{-1}+1)^{k_\\star}\n\\bigl(2^{-p_n}+2^{1-q_n}\\bigr).\n\\]\nEvery nonnegative radius recorded as a summand of either \\(\\Delta_n^{\\mathrm{enc}}\\) or \\(\\Delta_n^{\\mathrm{arith}}\\) obeys the corresponding upper bound.",
